# /new-view

## What This Does

Creates a new ERB view file for an existing controller action. Sets up the basic
layout, links to the controller's instance variables, and includes flash/error
boilerplate consistent with the project.

Use this when the controller already exists and you just need to add or replace
a view file.

## Usage

```
/new-view profiles index           # app/views/profiles/index.html.erb
/new-view admin/companies show     # app/views/admin/companies/show.html.erb
/new-view dashboard home           # app/views/dashboard/home.html.erb
```

## How It Works

### 1. Read Patterns

- `.claude/patterns/{{ 'patterns/rails-monolith-patterns.md' | installed(stack) }}`
- `.claude/patterns/{{ 'patterns/forms-patterns.md' | installed(stack) }}` (if generating new/edit)
- `.claude/styles/{{ 'styles/erb-style.md' | installed(stack) }}`

### 2. Verify the Controller and Action Exist

```bash
bin/rails routes | grep <resource>
```

If the route doesn't exist, suggest the route entry and stop.

### 3. Generate the View

#### `index.html.erb`

```erb
<% content_for :title, t('profiles.index.title') %>

<header class="{{ c.page_header }}">
  <h1 class="{{ c.h1 }}"><%= t('profiles.index.title') %></h1>
  <%= link_to t('profiles.index.new'), new_profile_path,
              class: "{{ v.css.button }}" %>
</header>

<% if @profiles.any? %>
  <ul class="{{ c.grid }}">
    <% @profiles.each do |profile| %>
      <li>
        <%= {{ card }} %>
      </li>
    <% end %>
  </ul>

  <%== pagy_nav(@pagy) if defined?(@pagy) %>
<% else %>
  <p class="{{ v.css.muted }}"><%= t('profiles.index.empty') %></p>
<% end %>
```

#### `show.html.erb`

```erb
<% content_for :title, @profile.name %>

{% if v.turbo %}
<%= turbo_frame_tag "profile_#{@profile.id}" do %>
{% else %}
<section id="profile_<%= @profile.id %>">
{% endif %}
  <%= {{ card_lg }} %>

  <div class="{{ c.actions }}">
    <%= link_to t('common.edit'), edit_profile_path(@profile),
                class: "{{ c.btn_secondary }}" %>
    <%= button_to t('common.destroy'), profile_path(@profile),
                  method: :delete,
                  {{ confirm }},
                  class: "{{ c.btn_danger }}" %>
  </div>
{% if v.turbo %}
<% end %>
{% else %}
</section>
{% endif %}
```

#### `new.html.erb` / `edit.html.erb`

```erb
<% content_for :title, t('profiles.new.title') %>

<h1 class="{{ c.h1_mb }}"><%= t('profiles.new.title') %></h1>

<%= render "form", profile: @profile %>
```

(Pair this with the `_form.html.erb` partial — see `/new-partial`{% if v.vc %} or `/new-form-component`{% endif %}.)

### 4. Suggest i18n Keys

Print the i18n keys to add to `config/locales/en.yml`:

```yaml
en:
  profiles:
    index:
      title: "Profiles"
      new: "New profile"
      empty: "No profiles yet."
    new:
      title: "New profile"
    create:
      success: "Profile created."
    update:
      success: "Profile updated."
    destroy:
      success: "Profile deleted."
```

### 5. Verify

```bash
# Render the page through a system spec or manually
bundle exec rails server
# Visit http://localhost:3000/profiles
```

## Rules

- Use `t('...')` for ALL user-visible strings — never hardcode English
{% if v.vc %}- Use ViewComponents for repeated UI; partials only for layout-y composition
{% elif v.phlex %}- Use Phlex components for repeated UI; partials only for layout-y composition
{% else %}- Extract repeated UI into partials with strict locals (`/new-partial`)
{% endif %}
- Use `content_for :title, ...` to set `<title>` from the layout
- Use `link_to` for navigation, `button_to` for state-changing actions
{% if v.turbo %}- Wrap edit-able sections in `turbo_frame_tag` if inline editing is desired
- Use `data: { turbo_confirm: t('...') }` for destructive confirmations
{% else %}- No Turbo here: confirm destructive actions with `form: { onsubmit: "return confirm(...)" }`{% if v.stim %} or a Stimulus controller{% endif %} (`data-turbo-confirm` does nothing without Turbo)
{% endif %}- Use semantic HTML: `<header>`, `<article>`, `<nav>`, `<section>`, `<main>`
- Always provide `alt` on images and labels on form fields

